<section class="section">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="kicker"><span>01</span>What it does</p>
    <h2>A radio that stays out of your way</h2>
    <p class="lead" style="margin-top:14px">One fixed key layout, the things you change most one press away, and the
      screen always telling you what the keys do next.</p>
    <div class="grid" style="margin-top:32px">
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Three slots, all listening</h3>
        <p>Slots A, B and C each hold a VFO or a channel. Watch listens to two or three of them while you talk on
          the one in front.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Transmit</h3>
        <p>FM voice on your region's amateur bands, with repeaters, tones, a tone search and a crossband
          repeater. If the radio won't transmit, it says why.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>APRS on the radio</h3>
        <p>Messages, beacons, stations heard with distance and direction, and a KISS TNC over the cable or
          Bluetooth. Slot C decodes it in the background.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Broadcast and shortwave</h3>
        <p>FM broadcast on any slot, with station text, while the others keep watching. HF mode for shortwave and
          AM.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>GPS and waypoints</h3>
        <p>Position, grid square, satellites, and waypoints with a dial that points the way. The GPS runs only
          while something needs it.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Battery life</h3>
        <p>The processor slows down while the radio waits, and Low Power Mode keeps only what you need to talk on
          one frequency.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p style="margin-top:24px"><a href="/features/">Every feature, in more detail</a></p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="kicker"><span>02</span>Measured</p>
    <h2>Numbers from the bench</h2>
    <p class="lead" style="margin-top:14px">Each one measured on our own radios and test audio, with the method
      written down.</p>
    <div class="figures">
      <div class="figure"><b>18.6 mA</b><span>at rest, against 64.7 mA with the processor at full speed all the time</span></div>
      <div class="figure"><b>107 hours</b><span>at rest on the stock battery pack, listening on a quiet channel: the processor runs at 24 MHz until something needs it</span></div>
      <div class="figure"><b>Top tier</b><span>APRS decoding inside the radio: 1,011 packets on the WA8LMF test CD, level with Dire Wolf on a PC</span></div>
      <div class="figure"><b>Within 4 %</b><span>of stock transmit power, at every level on 2 m and 70 cm</span></div>
    </div>
    <p style="margin-top:24px"><a href="/features/#measured">How these were measured</a></p>
  </div>
</section>

